WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.288
On the northern frontier, as the morning sun rose, Li Guang rode a fine horse with a longbow on his back, patrolling the border.

00:00:06.638 --> 00:00:09.950
The cold morning wind blew past, and his cloak fluttered softly.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:15.028
He bent his bow and nocked an arrow — his archery was superb, and every shot hit its mark.

00:00:15.378 --> 00:00:19.098
The soldiers gathered around, every one of them watching in amazement.

00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:24.176
When the Xiongnu scouts saw his banner, they turned and fled in fright — they called him the 'Flying General.'

00:00:24.526 --> 00:00:27.718
From then on, the frontier region spread the fame of the Flying General.

00:00:28.068 --> 00:00:33.900
When the court rewarded merit, the other generals were all made marquises — only Li Guang stood quietly to one side.

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:37.490
Li Guang lowered his head, unable to help feeling a little disappointed.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:43.648
As the years passed, Li Guang stood on the frontier, gazing at the sunset, his longbow still in his hand.

00:00:43.998 --> 00:00:46.926
He had guarded the frontier his whole life, and had never once flinched.

00:00:47.276 --> 00:00:52.724
Under the twinkling stars of the night sky, people forever remember the story of this Flying General.

00:00:53.074 --> 00:00:56.866
His story reminds us that talent and opportunity do not always arrive together.

